# MIDI in plays the Lead (after NACHTFAHRT's 9ae6dce): a note on any channel sounds on the Lead's channel 3 at the nearest
# note of the scale, the lower of two as near. The first piece is D Aeolian (D E F G A Bb C). The MIDI bytes are hex.
wait 500
expect pool 1453
# F4 (65, 0x41) is in the scale and sounds as played
midi 90 41 64
wait 300
expect lastnote_ch3 65
midi 80 41 00
wait 200
# F#4 (66, 0x42), between F and G: the lower, F
midi 90 42 64
wait 300
expect lastnote_ch3 65
midi 80 42 00
wait 200
# A4 (69, 0x45) on channel 5; a note on with velocity 0 is a note off
midi 94 45 5A
wait 300
expect lastnote_ch3 69
midi 94 45 00
wait 200
# G4 lights the fourth white key (w3, key 6), as the key itself does
midi 90 43 64
wait 300
expect litkey6 1
midi 80 43 00
wait 300
expect litkey6 0
# the note kept within the Lead's 36 .. 100
midi 90 00 64
wait 300
expect lastnote_ch3 36
midi 80 00 00
midi 90 7F 64
wait 300
expect lastnote_ch3 100
midi 80 7F 00
wait 200
# all notes off lets go of a MIDI note (the key's light again), not of a key held
midi 90 43 64
wait 300
expect litkey6 1
midi B0 7B 00
wait 300
expect litkey6 0
key w3 down
wait 300
expect litkey6 1
midi B0 7B 00
wait 300
expect litkey6 1
# nor does MIDI note 3's release let go of the key whose step is 3
midi 80 03 00
wait 300
expect litkey6 1
key w3 up
wait 300
expect litkey6 0
# the scale is the Key page's: never changed
expect pool 1453
